cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ObjectiveFrame in teaching, research, or published work, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "ObjectiveFrame: Interactive real-time finite element analysis for structural mechanics education"
authors:
  - family-names: Lindemann
    given-names: Jonas
repository-code: "https://github.com/jonaslindemann/objectiveframe"
url: "https://jonaslindemann.github.io/objectiveframe/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - finite element analysis
  - FEA
  - structural analysis
  - beam analysis
  - educational FEM
  - structural mechanics
  - eigenmode visualization
  - open-source software
abstract: >-
  ObjectiveFrame is an open-source interactive finite element analysis tool for
  beam and frame structures. It focuses on real-time structural feedback,
  educational finite element workflows, eigenmode visualization, and lightweight
  structural mechanics experimentation.
